<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32112" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">occŭbo</span></b> , āre, 1,
			v. n.
		ob-cubo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to lie</i> in a place; <i>to
			rest</i>, <i>repose</i> in the grave (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad tumulum, quo maximus occubat Hector,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 5, 371</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Paris urbe paternā occubat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 706</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crudelibus occubat umbris,</span>”
				<i>reposes with the dead</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 547</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flebili leto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Hippol. 997</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consul pro vestrā victoriā
					morte occubans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					8, 10, 4</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
